        <UserObject label="i get productID from payload.id and use that productID to get&amp;nbsp; the first 50 collections in which the current updated products exists using admin.graphql api&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;in response i get an array of collections (stored inside a variable named &quot;collections&quot;) and each array contains collection id and title&lt;/div&gt;" link="&#xa;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(255, 255, 255); font-family: Helvetica; font-size: 12px; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: center; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; white-space: normal; background-color: rgb(18, 18, 18); text-decoration-thickness: initial; text-decoration-style: initial; text-decoration-color: initial; display: inline !important; float: none;&quot;&gt;Now whenever merchants updates a product inventory, shopify sends a post request to my route webhooks.products-update.jsx&lt;/span&gt;&#xa;&#xa;" id="bdRQIAhR4CXSqjTb_yDt-22">
